    <section class="section" id="comparative-analysis">
      <span class="section-label">Strategy</span>
      <h2>Comparing and Combining Techniques</h2>
      <p>Each prompting paradigm excels in different scenarios. The art of prompt engineering is knowing which to deploy based on your task requirements, resource constraints, and performance targets.</p>

      <h3>Zero-Shot: When to Use</h3>
      <p>Zero-shot is ideal for initial prototyping, exploratory analysis, and tasks aligned with model training data. Use it when you need quick results with minimal setup. It's your first attempt; if performance is insufficient, then invest in few-shot or CoT.</p>

      <h3>Few-Shot: When to Use</h3>
      <p>Few-shot becomes essential for specialized domains, non-standard output formats, or production systems requiring consistency. If your task has unique characteristics or strict requirements, curating a few high-quality examples is well worth the effort. Few-shot typically provides 2-4x performance improvement over zero-shot on specialized tasks.</p>

      <h3>Chain-of-Thought: When to Use</h3>
      <p>CoT excels on reasoning-heavy tasks: math problems, logic puzzles, decision-making, multi-step analysis. If correctness and explanation are critical, CoT is your tool. It adds latency (more tokens generated) but dramatically improves accuracy on complex reasoning.</p>

      <h3>Hybrid Strategies</h3>
      <p>The most powerful prompts combine multiple techniques. For example, a few-shot chain-of-thought prompt combines guidance through examples with step-by-step reasoning:</p>

      <pre><code><span class="st">"You are a medical diagnostician. Analyze symptoms"</span>
<span class="st">"and suggest possible conditions. Show reasoning."</span>

<span class="st">"Example 1:"</span>
<span class="st">"Symptoms: High fever, cough, sore throat"</span>
<span class="st">"Reasoning: Classic respiratory symptoms, fever suggests"</span>
<span class="st">"infection. Duration?"</span>
<span class="st">"Likely conditions: Common cold, flu, strep throat"</span>

<span class="st">"Example 2:"</span>
<span class="st">"Symptoms: Chest pain, shortness of breath, dizziness"</span>
<span class="st">"Reasoning: Cardiac symptoms. Urgent evaluation needed."</span>
<span class="st">"Likely conditions: Angina, myocardial infarction, PE"</span>

<span class="st">"Symptoms: Joint pain, swelling, stiffness"</span>
<span class="st">"Reasoning:"</span></code></pre>

      <p>This hybrid approach leverages examples for domain guidance and chain-of-thought for thorough reasoning.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="practical-system">
      <span class="section-label">Implementation</span>
      <h2>Building a Complete Prompting System</h2>
      <p>Here's a production-ready Python class that implements all three prompting strategies with the OpenAI API:</p>

      <pre><code><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="nm">openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">OpenAI</span>
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="nm">enum</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">Enum</span>

<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="nm">PromptingStrategy</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">Enum</span><span class="op">):</span>
    <span class="nm">ZERO_SHOT</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"zero_shot"</span>
    <span class="nm">FEW_SHOT</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"few_shot"</span>
    <span class="nm">CHAIN_OF_THOUGHT</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"chain_of_thought"</span>
    <span class="nm">HYBRID</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"hybrid"</span>

<span class="kw">class</span> <span class="nm">TextClassifier</span><span class="op">:</span>
    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">api_key</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">api_key</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">api_key</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">classify</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">text</span><span class="op">,</span>
                  <span class="va">strategy</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">PromptingStrategy</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">ZERO_SHOT</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">strategy</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="nm">PromptingStrategy</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">ZERO_SHOT</span><span class="op">:</span>
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_zero_shot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">text</span><span class="op">)</span>
        <span class="kw">elif</span> <span class="va">strategy</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="nm">PromptingStrategy</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">FEW_SHOT</span><span class="op">:</span>
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_few_shot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">text</span><span class="op">)</span>
        <span class="kw">elif</span> <span class="va">strategy</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="nm">PromptingStrategy</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">CHAIN_OF_THOUGHT</span><span class="op">:</span>
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_cot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">text</span><span class="op">)</span>
        <span class="kw">else</span><span class="op">:</span>
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_hybrid</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">text</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_zero_shot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">text</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="nm">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">f</span><span class="st">"""Classify sentiment as positive, negative, or neutral.
Text: {text}
Sentiment:"""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_call_api</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">prompt</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_few_shot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">text</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="nm">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""Classify sentiment.
Ex1: Great product! → positive
Ex2: Terrible experience. → negative
Ex3: It works okay. → neutral
Text: """</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="nm">text</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="st">"""
Sentiment:"""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_call_api</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">prompt</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_cot</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">text</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="nm">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">f</span><span class="st">"""Analyze sentiment carefully. Show your reasoning.
Text: {text}
Analysis: Let me examine the emotional language..."""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_call_api</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">prompt</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_hybrid</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">text</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="nm">prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""Classify sentiment. Show reasoning.
Ex1: Great service! → positive (positive language)
Ex2: Terrible! → negative (strong negative words)
Text: """</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="nm">text</span> <span class="op">+</span> <span class="st">"""
Reasoning:"""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">_call_api</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="nm">prompt</span><span class="op">)</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_call_api</span><span class="op">(</span><span class="va">self</span><span class="op">,</span> <span class="va">prompt</span><span class="op">):</span>
        <span class="nm">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">client</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">chat</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">completions</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="fn">create</span><span class="op">(</span>
            <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="op">[{</span><span class="st">"role"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="st">"user"</span><span class="op">,</span>
                         <span class="st">"content"</span><span class="op">:</span> <span class="nm">prompt</span><span class="op">}],</span>
            <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0.0</span><span class="op">,</span>
            <span class="va">max_tokens</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">200</span>
        <span class="op">)</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="nm">response</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">choices</span><span class="op">[</span><span class="nm">0</span><span class="op">].</span><span class="nm">message</span><span class="op">.</span><span class="nm">content</span></code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="optimization">
      <span class="section-label">Best Practices</span>
      <h2>Optimizing and Evaluating Prompts</h2>
      <p>Effective prompt engineering requires systematic evaluation. Don't just assume a prompt works—measure its performance and iterate based on results.</p>

      <h3>Performance Metrics</h3>
      <p>Define how you'll measure success. For classification, use accuracy, precision, and recall. For generation tasks, use human evaluation or task-specific metrics. Document baseline performance from your zero-shot prompt, then measure improvements as you add examples or reasoning.</p>

      <h3>Iteration Process</h3>
      <p>Follow this workflow: (1) Start with a simple zero-shot prompt. (2) Measure performance. (3) If unsatisfactory, analyze failures to understand what's missing. (4) Add 2-3 strategically chosen examples targeting failure modes. (5) Re-measure and compare. (6) Continue refining based on results.</p>

      <h3>Example Curation</h3>
      <p>Don't randomly pick examples. Analyze model failures and select examples that address specific weaknesses. If the model struggles with edge cases, prioritize edge case examples. If output format is wrong, show format examples explicitly.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Professional Practice:</strong> Maintain a prompt versioning system. Document each prompt variant, its performance metrics, and the rationale for changes. This creates institutional knowledge and prevents regression.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="exercises">
      <span class="section-label">Practice</span>
      <h2>Hands-On Exercises</h2>

      <div class="exercise">
        <h4>Exercise 1: Zero-Shot Sentiment Analysis</h4>
        <p>Write a zero-shot prompt for sentiment classification. Test it on 10 diverse text samples (from very positive to very negative). Document accuracy and identify any failure cases. Why did those fail?</p>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise">
        <h4>Exercise 2: Few-Shot Example Design</h4>
        <p>Create a few-shot prompt with 3-4 examples for a task of your choice (entity extraction, intent classification, or content categorization). Carefully curate examples for diversity and quality. Compare performance against your zero-shot baseline.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise">
        <h4>Exercise 3: Chain-of-Thought on Math</h4>
        <p>Build a CoT prompt with 2 example problems and step-by-step solutions for math word problems. Test on 5 new problems. Measure accuracy compared to direct answering. Did reasoning steps improve performance?</p>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise">
        <h4>Exercise 4: Comparative Experiment</h4>
        <p>Implement all three strategies on the same task. Compare on accuracy, token count, and latency. Create a simple summary table showing which approach is best for your task and why.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="exercise">
        <h4>Exercise 5: Hybrid Prompt Design</h4>
        <p>Build a hybrid prompt combining few-shot examples with chain-of-thought reasoning for a complex task. Document how each component contributes to performance improvement.</p>
