    </section>

    <section class="section" id="summary">
      <h2 class="key-concept-header">Key Takeaways</h2>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Prompting Paradigms</h4>
        <p>Zero-shot is fast but limited. Few-shot adds precision through examples. Chain-of-thought improves reasoning. Choose based on task requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>In-Context Learning</h4>
        <p>Modern LLMs learn from examples in the context window itself, enabling rapid adaptation without training. This is a fundamental capability enabling few-shot and CoT prompting.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Example Quality Over Quantity</h4>
        <p>Two excellent examples outperform five mediocre ones. Focus on relevance, diversity, and correctness when curating few-shot examples.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Hybrid Approaches</h4>
        <p>Combining techniques creates powerful prompts. Few-shot chain-of-thought combines guidance through examples with step-by-step reasoning for maximum effectiveness.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <h4>Systematic Evaluation</h4>
        <p>Measure performance, iterate based on failures, and document improvements. Prompt engineering is experimental work; treat it as such.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

